// The Old Capital District (bible 4.7, 7.3 step 4, 5.4–5.6, 6.13, 6.14, 9). Corra's room (Capital_2): her drawing
// of her father keeps everyone out, him included (6.13). After it, Corra herself, if Wren looks: her memory can be
// carried out, which is what can turn Voss (5.5, 9.5). The mirror-Observatory (Capital_4): Corvin, the Archivist.
// He reveals 5.4 and 5.6 and lays out the choice. Wren can finish the Survey with him, or argue for giving the stones
// back. The argument is built from 5.3 (Ilse), 5.4 (his holding alone) and 5.6 (flight coming back through her).
// Win all three and he is persuaded (bible 9.2); the fight (6.14) happens either way.
// Corvin: grand, weary, self-correcting; "When I—"; does not say "it wasn't my fault".
// Corra: a heron chick; draws him bigger; does not say "gone".

title: Capital_Corra
---
<<if not has_flag("boss.corras_drawing.defeated")>>
    Corra: That's my father. He's coming. Don't. #still #face:wary #line:08a4c92
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("corra.decided")>>
    <<if has_flag("corra.memory_carried")>>
        Corra: Did you give it him yet? He'll say it's the wrong size. It isn't. #still #face:asking #line:099d12f
    <<else>>
        Corra: I'm drawing him again. Smaller this time. So he fits through the door. #still #face:grave #line:0161951
    <<endif>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Corra: I drew him bigger. He was bigger. #face:grave #line:0448105
Corra: He's the Guildmaster now. I know. I drew that too. He doesn't come in. #reveal:5.5 #face:grave #line:0ad196d
Corra: Is that him? Behind you? Is he here? #line:06fb921
-> Let me carry this to him. #line:08db476
    <<voice warden blank>>
    <<jump Capital_Corra_Carry>>
-> What's his name? #line:0241c5d
    Corra: Papa. And Aurelian, when he's in trouble. #callback:5.5 #face:bright #line:0f51ea1
    Corra: Will you take him this? It's a small one. The big one's for keeping people out. #face:asking #line:0770867
    <<voice surveyor blank>>
    -> Yes. I'll take it. #line:01f46c1
        <<voice warden blank>>
        <<jump Capital_Corra_Carry>>
    -> Not yet. #line:0b95001
        <<voice surveyor blank>>
        Corra: Then I'll keep drawing. I've got lots of paper. It's all paper here. #face:grave #line:0d80cef
-> ... #line:011f622
    Corra: You're like him. He doesn't talk either. #face:grave #line:002d1ac
    <<voice drift blank>>
<<flag corra.decided 1>>
===

title: Capital_Corra_Carry
---
Corra: Here. The small one. It's the right size. #face:bright #line:067d85a
Corra: Tell him I kept drawing. Tell him the crayon ran out and I did it in outline. #face:grave #line:0c957c3
<<flag corra.memory_carried 1>>
<<flag corra.decided 1>>
===

title: Capital_Corvin
---
<<if has_flag("boss.archivist.defeated")>>
    <<jump Capital_Corvin_After>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("capital.corvin.spoken")>>
    Corvin: When I— sit. The chair is still there. It will be there after, too. #still #face:grave #line:0e8a184
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Corvin: When I— granddaughter. Sit. I have drawn you a chair. #reveal:5.4 #face:bright #line:07b2ab1
Corvin: The night it broke, I walked in looking for my wife and my daughter. #face:grave #line:06de41d
Corvin: I held on so hard the Hollow went under with me. Ilse's village. Yours. #face:grave #line:0a77e3e
Corvin: Halloway. It's yours. Isolde gave it to you so you could come and ask me for it. #line:0c38a1c
Corvin: And the sky. When I— the sky was in the Atlas, like everything else. #line:0699ef1
Corvin: When it broke, you forgot it. Nobody lost their wings. They lost the memory of them. #reveal:5.6 #face:grave #line:0e26bc8
Corvin: It comes back through you. Both worlds. That is why the old flight finds you, piece by piece. #line:0332b7b
Corvin: Seven stones and the Atlas is whole. Nothing fades. The sky stays held, safe, for everyone. #face:bright #line:03f700f
<<sing archivist>>
Corvin: Or give them back, and hope. I have hoped for forty-one years. It is overrated. #face:wary #line:002f4f7
-> Finish the Survey with you. #line:08aafef
    Corvin: Good. Good. Bring them to the frame. I will show you where each one sits. #face:bright #line:0ca2ce4
    <<flag corvin.stance 1>>
    <<voice warden blank>>
-> Give them back. All of them. #line:0336357
    <<voice surveyor blank>>
    <<jump Capital_Corvin_Argue>>
-> ... #line:0aa15d3
    Corvin: Then think. I drew you a chair for thinking. #line:0becbc9
    <<voice drift blank>>
<<flag capital.corvin.spoken 1>>
===

title: Capital_Corvin_Argue
---
Corvin: Give them back? When I— Ilse fades. Do you want your mother to fade? #face:wary #line:0b8c8bc
-> She let me go. She'd let this go. <<if has_flag("blank.ilse.heard")>> #line:0d8b46d
    <<voice drift blank>>
    Corvin: She would. She did. She let me go too, and I didn't let her. #face:grave #line:038963d
    <<flag corvin.argued_ilse 1>>
-> She's already faded. #line:0e0457b
    <<voice surveyor blank>>
    Corvin: So she has. And you'd leave her so. Hm. #face:wary #line:0a06c58
-> ... #line:08057ab
    <<voice drift blank>>
    Corvin: Silence is not an answer, granddaughter. It is a chair. #face:wary #line:0da24ce
Corvin: The Hollow went under because I held. And you would have me hold nothing? #face:wary #line:0c46286
-> You held alone. That pulled it under. #line:090f081
    <<voice surveyor blank>>
    Corvin: Alone. When I— yes. There was nobody else walking it. Nobody singing. #face:grave #line:02351f4
    <<flag corvin.argued_alone 1>>
-> Then hold everything. #line:0da2c70
    <<voice warden blank>>
    Corvin: That is my argument, not yours. Try again, later. #face:wary #line:0a70fb1
-> You couldn't have known. #line:01d9273
    <<voice drift blank>>
    Corvin: Don't. Somebody has to have done it. It was me. #face:grave #line:024d82f
Corvin: And the sky? Break the frame and it scatters. Nobody holds it whole again. #face:wary #line:0a2c2cb
-> It came back to me. Not the Atlas. <<if has_flag("windreach.leap.done")>> #line:0b64759
    <<voice surveyor blank>>
    Corvin: At the Wind Gate. I heard. The whole Steppe heard. Forty years, and then you. #face:bright #line:0702f18
    <<flag corvin.argued_sky 1>>
-> Then let it scatter. #line:078b10b
    <<voice drift blank>>
    Corvin: You say it so lightly. You've flown. #face:wary #line:08b986f
-> ... #line:0036742
    <<voice drift blank>>
    Corvin: Hm. #face:wary #line:0040d49
<<if has_flag("corvin.argued_ilse") and has_flag("corvin.argued_alone") and has_flag("corvin.argued_sky")>>
    Corvin: When I— you are young, and you might be right. I am old. Show me. #face:grave #line:0e7f2a9
    <<flag corvin.stance 2>>
<<elseif can_offer("archivist", "isolde.first_sight")>>
    Corvin: No. You are young, and you are wrong. When I— you carry something of hers. #face:wary #line:0f48caf
    Corvin: The first time she saw you. Give it to me. Let me see what she saw. #face:asking #line:096f7c4
    -> Take it. Look at me. Only at me. #line:0ffdbc1
        <<voice warden blank>>
        <<offer archivist isolde.first_sight>>
        Corvin: When I— a child at the edge of the white. Looking straight at her. Oh. #face:grave #line:00a8376
        Corvin: You are young, and you might be right. I am old. Show me. #face:grave #line:0993981
        <<flag corvin.stance 2>>
    -> It's mine. She gave it to me. #line:0000fce
        <<voice surveyor blank>>
        Corvin: Then keep it. Somebody should. No. Sit. I love you. #face:grave #line:0c1d882
        <<flag corvin.stance 3>>
    -> ... #line:0326d66
        <<voice drift blank>>
        Corvin: Silence, and you keep it. The chair, then. Sit. #face:grave #line:0c5839a
        <<flag corvin.stance 3>>
<<else>>
    Corvin: No. You are young, and you are wrong, and I love you. Sit. #face:grave #line:023f34e
    <<flag corvin.stance 3>>
<<endif>>
<<flag capital.corvin.spoken 1>>
===

title: Capital_Corvin_After
---
<<if has_flag("capital.corvin.after")>>
    Corvin: Back? The chair is still here. Go on, then. Say it. #face:asking #line:0c6c275
    -> Let's finish your Survey. <<if flag("corvin.stance") != 1>> #line:030323d
        <<voice warden blank>>
        Corvin: Good. Good. Bring them to the frame. #face:bright #line:033ad88
        <<flag corvin.stance 1>>
    -> Hear me out again. <<if flag("corvin.stance") != 2>> #line:0115589
        <<voice surveyor blank>>
        <<jump Capital_Corvin_Argue>>
    -> I'll sit. I'll draw with you. <<if ending_open("rest")>> #line:06da95d
        <<voice drift blank>>
        <<jump Ending_Rest>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Corvin: Then draw it better than I did. Go on. #face:grave #line:06cc429
<<if keystones() == 0>>
    Corvin: You carry none. Nobody's stones at all. Then there is a third way. #line:0030486
    Corvin: Stay. Sit in the chair. Draw with me. Nobody will hold you to anything. #face:bright #line:059ef79
    <<flag ending.rest_offered 1>>
    -> Keep your stone. I'll think. #line:0c1bb4a
        Corvin: Thinking is allowed. The chair is good for it. #face:bright #line:0ccf293
        <<voice drift blank>>
    -> Give it to me. #line:0607af7
        Corvin: The seventh. Heavier than it looks. They all are. #face:grave #line:0008744
        <<flag keystone.archivist 1>>
        <<voice warden blank>>
<<else>>
    Corvin: The seventh. Take it. Whatever you mean to do with it. Heavier than it looks. #face:grave #line:0ff5881
    <<flag keystone.archivist 1>>
<<endif>>
<<flag capital.corvin.after 1>>
===

title: Ending_Rest
---
// The Cartographer's Rest (bible 9.4, secret): zero anchors, zero stones, and the chair. Isolde goes free in trade.
Corvin: Sit. The chair is yours. I drew it before you were born. #face:bright #line:0d95fe4
Corvin: Isolde can go. I'll have the white let go of her. That's the trade, if you like. #line:0228c30
Mirror: She sits in the mirror-Observatory and draws. Corvin draws beside her. #line:0c76c01
Corvin: When I— no. Nothing. Draw. #face:grave #line:0490017
<<flag ending.chosen 4>>
<<flag ending.rest 1>>
<<epilogue>>
===

title: Capital_Marrow_Word
---
<<if flag("marrow.words") >= 2>>
    Lantern: The grey chick, one pace back, one to the left. #still #line:00e7cb5
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if not has_flag("capital.corvin.spoken") or flag("marrow.words") < 1>>
    Lantern: The grey chick looks up at the mirror-dome and says nothing. #still #line:0b6c82b
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Corvin: When I— I held it. I held all of it. Nothing was lost. #face:wary #line:0dcf39b
Marrow: Nothing was lost. #echo:corvin #line:0842c49
Corvin: You see? Even the child. #face:bright #line:0e95dac
Marrow: Lost. #echo:corvin #line:0c28f3f
Marrow: Up. #line:0c4d954
<<flag marrow.words 2>>
===
